.SH NAME
Plack::Session::Store::Null \- Null store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 3
\&  use Plack::Builder;
\&  use Plack::Middleware::Session;
\&  use Plack::Session::Store::Null;
\&
\&  my $app = sub {
\&      return [ 200, [ \*(AqContent\-Type\*(Aq => \*(Aqtext/plain\*(Aq ], [ \*(AqHello Foo\*(Aq ] ];
\&  };
\&
\&  builder {
\&      enable \*(AqSession\*(Aq,
\&          store => Plack::Session::Store::Null\->new;
\&      $app;
\&  };
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Sometimes you don't want to store anything in your sessions, but
Plack::Session requires a \f(CW\*(C`store\*(C'\fR instance, so you can use this
one and all methods will return null.
.PP
This is a subclass of Plack::Session::Store and implements
its full interface.
